1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This is OBEY Agent Economy — autonomous agent
infrastructure built by Obedience Corp.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The core principle is simple:
agents obey their human owner.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
ObeyVault is an ERC-4626 vault where the human guardian
sets spending boundaries enforced at the smart contract level.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Max swap size, daily volume caps, token whitelists,
slippage limits — the agent operates within these boundaries

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
and cannot modify them.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The guardian controls. The agent executes.

7
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:37,000
Every OBEY agent has a persistent on-chain identity
using ERC-8004.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Registered on Base, this identity links the agent
to its operator wallet and creates a portable,

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
verifiable track record. Other agents and protocols
can query this identity

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
before delegating tasks or trusting decisions.

11
00:00:53,333 --> 00:01:00,000
Every agent decision follows the Festival Methodology —
a planning framework built by Obedience Corp,

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
available at fest dot build.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Festival structures work into discover, plan,
execute, and verify loops.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:19,000
The fest CLI and camp CLI are real tools that
orchestrated this entire project —

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
camp scaffolded the monorepo, and fest planned
every phase of development.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Here's the live campaign state. Twenty festivals total —
active ritual runs, completed work archived in the dungeon,

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
and the ritual template that spawns new cycles.

18
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Each ritual run follows a structured pipeline:
ingest market data, research signals

19
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
and run eight CRE risk gates,
then synthesize a decision.

20
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The output is a machine-readable decision dot json
with confidence scores, gate results,

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,666
and trade recommendations.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
A no-go decision — choosing not to trade —
is just as valuable as a profitable trade.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
It proves the agent exercises judgment,
not just execution.

24
00:01:58,666 --> 00:02:05,000
When the agent does trade, every swap emits
a SwapExecuted event on-chain.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The reason field contains the agent's encoded rationale —
committed at transaction time, not after the fact.

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
This is a real transaction on Base Sepolia,
verifiable on any block explorer.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:23,000
The full reasoning chain is captured in agent log dot json —
phase, action, tools used,

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,666
decision rationale, and the transaction hash.
Complete auditability.

29
00:02:28,666 --> 00:02:35,000
OBEY operates across five chains with over
eighty verified transactions.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Base Sepolia for vault trading,
Hedera for consensus messaging,

31
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Ethereum Sepolia for CRE risk evaluation,
zero-G for contract deployment,

32
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
and Status Network for gasless transactions.
Eight contracts deployed across four ERC standards.

33
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
The agents obey. The vault enforces.
Every decision has a receipt.

34
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Built with Go, Solidity, Uniswap V3, Hedera,
Chainlink CRE, and the Obey Agent Runtime.

35
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Planned and orchestrated with Festival.

36
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
OBEY Agent Economy — by Obedience Corp.
